docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/R55.log:11:{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0156xfMwYhJkhkYBemq1yMXu","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# R55 — Contract gate — Memory ↔ Verification ↔ Retrieval cross-layer\n2\t\n3\t**Phase:** cross-layer (gates 7 → 8)\n4\t**Type:** review\n5\t**Model class:** advanced\n6\t**Depends on:** R25, R33, R54\n7\t**Spec anchor:** [§Memory Graph](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#4-memory-graph), [§Verification Engine](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#8-verification-engine), [§Retrieval Engine](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#7-retrieval-engine), [§Non-Negotiable Product Properties](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#non-negotiable-product-properties)\n8\t**Standards:** Cadres coding standard; Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n9\t\n10\t## Goal\n11\t\n12\tThis task is the cross-layer contract gate between the Memory Graph (R25, Phase 3), the Retrieval Engine (R33, Phase 4), and the Verification Engine (R54, Phase 7). It proves that the three subsystems agree on three contract surfaces — `VerificationStatus` round-trips losslessly between memory and verification; `ScopeFilter` reaches every retrieval path; and `BundleProducer` / `SurfacedBundle` (T52) is the single way retrieval surfaces memory results — and that none of the three Phase 8 workflow tools can ship until the contracts hold. The review ships a new contract test file under `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/contract_tests/` that exercises all three round-trips end-to-end against the real subsystems.\n13\t\n14\t## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n15\t\n16\t> §Non-Negotiable Product Properties: \"Every retrieved memory has an inclusion reason. Every stale or contradicted memory is surfaced as such, not hidden behind recency.\"\n17\t\n18\t> §Verification Engine outputs: `verified`, `unverified`, `in_review`, `stale`, `contradicted`, `superseded`, `expired`, `invalidated`.\n19\t\n20\t> §Risks — Scope Leakage: \"scope-aware queries, enforced filters in store APIs, and negative tests.\"\n21\t\n22\t> §Retrieval Engine: \"Ranking signals: ... verification status; freshness; scope; ... contradiction/supersession state ...\"\n23\t\n24\t## Inputs\n25\t\n26\t- Dependency outputs: R25 (Phase 3 memory graph review), R33 (Phase 4 retrieval review), R54 (Phase 7 verification review). All three must pass for this gate.\n27\t- Existing repo files this task reviews:\n28\t  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory/` — `VerificationStatus` column, `ScopeFilter` plumbing.\n29\t  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/verification/` — verifier verdicts and the `BundleProducer` contract.\n30\t  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/query/` — retrieval pipeline; must consume `ScopeFilter` and produce results via `BundleProducer`.\n31\t  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/intelligence/` — workflow tools that compose retrieval results into bundles.\n32\t- Standards: Cadres coding standard §Single source of truth, §Tests as documentation, §Done means done; Lattice rules on doc-heading citation.\n33\t\n34\t## Steps\n35\t\n36\t1. Read spec §Memory Graph, §Retrieval Engine, §Verification Engine, and §Non-Negotiable Product Properties in full. Copy the relevant bullets into the top-of-file doc comment on `contract_tests/memory_verification_retrieval.rs`.\n37\t2. Identify the three contract surfaces explicitly:\n38\t   - **VerificationStatus round-trip:** every `VerificationStatus` value persisted by the verifier (T48–T51) deserializes losslessly from `memories.verification_status` and matches the same enum variant in retrieval's ranker (Phase 4).\n39\t   - **ScopeFilter round-trip:** every retrieval entry point requires a `ScopeFilter` and applies it through `MemoryStore::list_memories(filter, …)` — no public retrieval API may accept a request without a filter.\n40\t   - **SurfacedBundle round-trip:** every retrieval result that touches durable memory passes through `SurfacingPipeline::partition` (T52); no caller composes a trusted/advisory split independently.\n41\t3. Create `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/contract_tests/` (and `mod.rs`) if absent, registered under `#[cfg(test)]` in `lib.rs`.\n42\t4. Author `contract_tests/memory_verification_retrieval.rs` with a fixture harness seeding the full Phase 3 + Phase 4 + Phase 7 stack against a temp SQLite store. The fixture seeds memories spanning every `VerificationStatus`, every scope, and a mix of evidence kinds (file / symbol / doc / test) so contract checks have material to assert on.\n43\t5. Write `test_verification_status_round_trip_memory_to_retrieval`: persist a memory in each of the eight `VerificationStatus` variants, run a retrieval query, assert each memory's status in the retrieval result equals the persisted value (no silent state mapping).\n44\t6. Write `test_scope_filter_round_trip_for_all_scope_kinds`: for each scope (session / branch / repo / organization), construct a non-matching `ScopeFilter`, call the retrieval API, assert zero leaked rows and a `MemoryScopeFiltered` event per attempt.\n45\t7. Write `test_stale_label_round_trip_retrieval_to_surfaced_bundle`: seed `Stale`, `Contradicted`, `Superseded`, `Expired`, `Invalidated` memories, run the retrieval pipeline, assert none appear in `SurfacedBundle.trusted` and each appears in `SurfacedBundle.advisory` with the matching `BundleSection` and a non-empty `label_reason`.\n46\t8. Write `test_retrieval_api_requires_scope_filter_argument`: a compile-time test (using `compile_fail` doctests or a `trybuild` fixture) that confirms the public retrieval entry point fails to compile without a `ScopeFilter`. If `trybuild` is unavailable in this crate, fall back to a runtime test asserting every public retrieval function in `query::engine` has a `ScopeFilter`-typed parameter (via reflection / a manually maintained list audited in this test).\n47\t9. Run `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib contract_tests::memory_verification_retrieval` and capture the results in the review.\n48\t10. Write the review at `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R55-contract-memory-verification-retrieval.md` with the mandatory headings: `## Contract surfaces`, `## Round-trip evidence`, `## Stale-label round-trip`, `## Scope-filter round-trip`, `## Findings`, `## Verdict`. `## Contract surfaces` enumerates the three contract surfaces and the code paths that implement them. `## Round-trip evidence`, `## Stale-label round-trip`, and `## Scope-filter round-trip` each cite the matching contract test and its assertions. `## Verdict` states `pass` or `fail` with one-paragraph justification.\n49\t\n50\t## Files expected\n51\t\n52\t- `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R55-contract-memory-verification-retrieval.md` — cross-layer contract review with all six mandatory headings, concrete evidence per section, pass/fail verdict.\n53\t- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/contract_tests/memory_verification_retrieval.rs` — contract round-trip tests for `VerificationStatus`, `ScopeFilter`, and `SurfacedBundle` across the memory / verification / retrieval subsystems.\n54\t\n55\t## Verification\n56\t\n57\t- `test -f docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R55-contract-memory-verification-retrieval.md` — confirms the review file exists.\n58\t- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/contract_tests/memory_verification_retrieval.rs` — confirms the contract test file exists at the canonical path.\n59\t- `grep -q '## Contract surfaces' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R55-contract-memory-verification-retrieval.md` — `## Contract surfaces` heading present.\n60\t- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib contract_tests::memory_verification_retrieval` — every contract round-trip test passes.\n61\t\n62\t## Coding-standard checks\n63\t\n64\t- File length ≤800 lines per file (review doc and test file).\n65\t- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10 for any helper in the contract test file. Tests themselves ≤30 lines.\n66\t- Single source of truth: contract tests exercise the real subsystem APIs — `MemoryStore::list_memories`, `query::engine` retrieval entry points, `SurfacingPipeline::partition` — never re-implement filtering or surfacing.\n67\t- Naming: contract tests follow `test_<contract>_round_trip_<scope>` (e.g. `test_scope_filter_round_trip_for_all_scope_kinds`).\n68\t- Error handling: tests assert on typed outcomes (`BundleSection`, `VerificationStatus` variants, `MemoryScopeFiltered` events).\n69\t- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code, or unjustified `#[allow(...)]`.\n70\t- Observability: tests capture `tracing` output where assertions involve log lines (e.g. `scope_leak_blocked`).\n71\t- Doc citation: review and test file cite the spec headings §Memory Graph, §Retrieval Engine, §Verification Engine, §Non-Negotiable Product Properties (per `lattice/CLAUDE.md` § Markdown Heading References).\n72\t\n73\t## Definition of done\n74\t\n75\t- [ ] `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R55-contract-memory-verification-retrieval.md` exists with all six mandatory headings.\n76\t- [ ] `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/contract_tests/memory_verification_retrieval.rs` exists with every contract test from steps 5–8 implemented.\n77\t- [ ] Every verification command passes from repo root.\n78\t- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n79\t- [ ] No deferred work: all three contract surfaces (status, scope-filter, surfaced-bundle) are covered end-to-end. If any retrieval entry point bypasses `ScopeFilter` or `SurfacingPipeline::partition`, the review's `## Findings` lists the violation and `## Verdict` is `fail` with a minimum-fix task list.\n80\t- [ ] If the verdict is `fail`, Phase 8 work (T56+) MUST NOT begin until the listed fixes are completed and R55 is rerun.\n81\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"623701ab-dc49-4054-96ef-292da32369e2","uuid":"9d36dcad-a607-4d34-a036-64a542779403","timestamp":"2026-05-17T13:08:56.778Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/R55.md","content":"# R55 — Contract gate — Memory ↔ Verification ↔ Retrieval cross-layer\n\n**Phase:** cross-layer (gates 7 → 8)\n**Type:** review\n**Model class:** advanced\n**Depends on:** R25, R33, R54\n**Spec anchor:** [§Memory Graph](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#4-memory-graph), [§Verification Engine](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#8-verification-engine), [§Retrieval Engine](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#7-retrieval-engine), [§Non-Negotiable Product Properties](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#non-negotiable-product-properties)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard; Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task is the cross-layer contract gate between the Memory Graph (R25, Phase 3), the Retrieval Engine (R33, Phase 4), and the Verification Engine (R54, Phase 7). It proves that the three subsystems agree on three contract surfaces — `VerificationStatus` round-trips losslessly between memory and verification; `ScopeFilter` reaches every retrieval path; and `BundleProducer` / `SurfacedBundle` (T52) is the single way retrieval surfaces memory results — and that none of the three Phase 8 workflow tools can ship until the contracts hold. The review ships a new contract test file under `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/contract_tests/` that exercises all three round-trips end-to-end against the real subsystems.\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> §Non-Negotiable Product Properties: \"Every retrieved memory has an inclusion reason. Every stale or contradicted memory is surfaced as such, not hidden behind recency.\"\n\n> §Verification Engine outputs: `verified`, `unverified`, `in_review`, `stale`, `contradicted`, `superseded`, `expired`, `invalidated`.\n\n> §Risks — Scope Leakage: \"scope-aware queries, enforced filters in store APIs, and negative tests.\"\n\n> §Retrieval Engine: \"Ranking signals: ... verification status; freshness; scope; ... contradiction/supersession state ...\"\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs: R25 (Phase 3 memory graph review), R33 (Phase 4 retrieval review), R54 (Phase 7 verification review). All three must pass for this gate.\n- Existing repo files this task reviews:\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory/` — `VerificationStatus` column, `ScopeFilter` plumbing.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/verification/` — verifier verdicts and the `BundleProducer` contract.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/query/` — retrieval pipeline; must consume `ScopeFilter` and produce results via `BundleProducer`.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/intelligence/` — workflow tools that compose retrieval results into bundles.\n- Standards: Cadres coding standard §Single source of truth, §Tests as documentation, §Done means done; Lattice rules on doc-heading citation.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Read spec §Memory Graph, §Retrieval Engine, §Verification Engine, and §Non-Negotiable Product Properties in full. Copy the relevant bullets into the top-of-file doc comment on `contract_tests/memory_verification_retrieval.rs`.\n2. Identify the three contract surfaces explicitly:\n   - **VerificationStatus round-trip:** every `VerificationStatus` value persisted by the verifier (T48–T51) deserializes losslessly from `memories.verification_status` and matches the same enum variant in retrieval's ranker (Phase 4).\n   - **ScopeFilter round-trip:** every retrieval entry point requires a `ScopeFilter` and applies it through `MemoryStore::list_memories(filter, …)` — no public retrieval API may accept a request without a filter.\n   - **SurfacedBundle round-trip:** every retrieval result that touches durable memory passes through `SurfacingPipeline::partition` (T52); no caller composes a trusted/advisory split independently.\n3. Create `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/contract_tests/` (and `mod.rs`) if absent, registered under `#[cfg(test)]` in `lib.rs`.\n4. Author `contract_tests/memory_verification_retrieval.rs` with a fixture harness seeding the full Phase 3 + Phase 4 + Phase 7 stack against a temp SQLite store. The fixture seeds memories spanning every `VerificationStatus`, every scope, and a mix of evidence kinds (file / symbol / doc / test) so contract checks have material to assert on.\n5. Write `test_verification_status_round_trip_memory_to_retrieval`: persist a memory in each of the eight `VerificationStatus` variants, run a retrieval query, assert each memory's status in the retrieval result equals the persisted value (no silent state mapping).\n6. Write `test_scope_filter_round_trip_for_all_scope_kinds`: for each scope (session / branch / repo / organization), construct a non-matching `ScopeFilter`, call the retrieval API, assert zero leaked rows and a `MemoryScopeFiltered` event per attempt.\n7. Write `test_stale_label_round_trip_retrieval_to_surfaced_bundle`: seed `Stale`, `Contradicted`, `Superseded`, `Expired`, `Invalidated` memories, run the retrieval pipeline, assert none appear in `SurfacedBundle.trusted` and each appears in `SurfacedBundle.advisory` with the matching `BundleSection` and a non-empty `label_reason`.\n8. Write `test_retrieval_api_requires_scope_filter_argument`: a compile-time test (using `compile_fail` doctests or a `trybuild` fixture) that confirms the public retrieval entry point fails to compile without a `ScopeFilter`. If `trybuild` is unavailable in this crate, fall back to a runtime test asserting every public retrieval function in `query::engine` has a `ScopeFilter`-typed parameter (via reflection / a manually maintained list audited in this test).\n9. Run `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib contract_tests::memory_verification_retrieval` and capture the results in the review.\n10. Write the review at `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R55-contract-memory-verification-retrieval.md` with the mandatory headings: `## Contract surfaces`, `## Round-trip evidence`, `## Stale-label round-trip`, `## Scope-filter round-trip`, `## Findings`, `## Verdict`. `## Contract surfaces` enumerates the three contract surfaces and the code paths that implement them. `## Round-trip evidence`, `## Stale-label round-trip`, and `## Scope-filter round-trip` each cite the matching contract test and its assertions. `## Verdict` states `pass` or `fail` with one-paragraph justification.\n\n## Files expected\n\n- `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R55-contract-memory-verification-retrieval.md` — cross-layer contract review with all six mandatory headings, concrete evidence per section, pass/fail verdict.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/contract_tests/memory_verification_retrieval.rs` — contract round-trip tests for `VerificationStatus`, `ScopeFilter`, and `SurfacedBundle` across the memory / verification / retrieval subsystems.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R55-contract-memory-verification-retrieval.md` — confirms the review file exists.\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/contract_tests/memory_verification_retrieval.rs` — confirms the contract test file exists at the canonical path.\n- `grep -q '## Contract surfaces' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R55-contract-memory-verification-retrieval.md` — `## Contract surfaces` heading present.\n- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib contract_tests::memory_verification_retrieval` — every contract round-trip test passes.\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines per file (review doc and test file).\n- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10 for any helper in the contract test file. Tests themselves ≤30 lines.\n- Single source of truth: contract tests exercise the real subsystem APIs — `MemoryStore::list_memories`, `query::engine` retrieval entry points, `SurfacingPipeline::partition` — never re-implement filtering or surfacing.\n- Naming: contract tests follow `test_<contract>_round_trip_<scope>` (e.g. `test_scope_filter_round_trip_for_all_scope_kinds`).\n- Error handling: tests assert on typed outcomes (`BundleSection`, `VerificationStatus` variants, `MemoryScopeFiltered` events).\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code, or unjustified `#[allow(...)]`.\n- Observability: tests capture `tracing` output where assertions involve log lines (e.g. `scope_leak_blocked`).\n- Doc citation: review and test file cite the spec headings §Memory Graph, §Retrieval Engine, §Verification Engine, §Non-Negotiable Product Properties (per `lattice/CLAUDE.md` § Markdown Heading References).\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R55-contract-memory-verification-retrieval.md` exists with all six mandatory headings.\n- [ ] `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/contract_tests/memory_verification_retrieval.rs` exists with every contract test from steps 5–8 implemented.\n- [ ] Every verification command passes from repo root.\n- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n- [ ] No deferred work: all three contract surfaces (status, scope-filter, surfaced-bundle) are covered end-to-end. If any retrieval entry point bypasses `ScopeFilter` or `SurfacingPipeline::partition`, the review's `## Findings` lists the violation and `## Verdict` is `fail` with a minimum-fix task list.\n- [ ] If the verdict is `fail`, Phase 8 work (T56+) MUST NOT begin until the listed fixes are completed and R55 is rerun.\n","numLines":81,"startLine":1,"totalLines":81}}}
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/R55.log:27:{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DwT8oz4wE4T1XDeGS4GPuh","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t//! Shared fixtures, harness, and identity factories for the R26 cross-layer\n2\t//! contract tests in `identity_event_memory.rs`.\n3\t//!\n4\t//! These helpers exist so the test file can stay focused on the contract\n5\t//! surfaces it pins. Per the Cadres coding standard `## Hard limits`, this\n6\t//! support module keeps the test file under the 800-line ceiling without\n7\t//! losing the per-surface organization that makes the gate readable.\n8\t\n9\tuse std::collections::HashMap;\n10\tuse std::sync::{Arc, Mutex};\n11\t\n12\tuse rusqlite::Connection;\n13\tuse tempfile::TempDir;\n14\t\n15\tuse crate::events::{\n16\t    Actor, EventEnvelope, EventQuery, EventReader, EventStore, EventWriter, FlushPolicy,\n17\t    PartialEnvelope, QueryOrder,\n18\t};\n19\tuse crate::graph::CodeGraph;\n20\tuse crate::identity::{\n21\t    ContextHandleId, DocId, EventId, FileId, IdentityResolver, MemoryId, SectionId, SymbolId,\n22\t};\n23\tuse crate::memory_graph::store::MemoryScopeState;\n24\tuse crate::memory_graph::{\n25\t    initialize_schema, AssertionType, EvidenceAnchor, FreshnessKind, FreshnessPolicy,\n26\t    IdempotencyKey, MemoryClass, MemoryDraft, MemoryEvidence, MemoryEvidenceId, MemoryScope,\n27\t    MemoryStore,\n28\t};\n29\tuse crate::parser::parse_file;\n30\tuse crate::storage::graph_store::{\n31\t    FileIndexEntry, FILE_INDEX_PARSER_VERSION, FILE_INDEX_SCHEMA_VERSION,\n32\t};\n33\tuse crate::DateTime;\n34\t\n35\tpub(super) const WORKSPACE: &str = \"workspace\";\n36\tpub(super) const BRANCH: &str = \"main\";\n37\tpub(super) const SESSION: &str = \"contract-session\";\n38\t\n39\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n40\t// Identity factories\n41\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n42\t\n43\tpub(super) fn file_identity(path: &str) -> FileId {\n44\t    FileId {\n45\t        workspace_id: WORKSPACE.to_string(),\n46\t        repo_relative_path: path.to_string(),\n47\t        content_hash: \"feedface00000001\".to_string(),\n48\t    }\n49\t}\n50\t\n51\tpub(super) fn doc_identity(path: &str) -> DocId {\n52\t    DocId {\n53\t        workspace_id: WORKSPACE.to_string(),\n54\t        repo_relative_path: path.to_string(),\n55\t        content_hash: \"deadbeef00000002\".to_string(),\n56\t    }\n57\t}\n58\t\n59\tpub(super) fn section_identity(path: &str, heading: &str) -> SectionId {\n60\t    SectionId {\n61\t        doc: doc_identity(path),\n62\t        heading_path: vec![heading.to_string()],\n63\t        byte_offset: 64,\n64\t    }\n65\t}\n66\t\n67\tpub(super) fn symbol_identity(file: &FileId, qualified: &str) -> SymbolId {\n68\t    SymbolId {\n69\t        file: file.clone(),\n70\t        qualified_name: qualified.to_string(),\n71\t        byte_offset: 12,\n72\t        kind: \"function\".to_string(),\n73\t    }\n74\t}\n75\t\n76\tpub(super) fn context_handle_identity(seed: &str) -> ContextHandleId {\n77\t    ContextHandleId {\n78\t        workspace_id: WORKSPACE.to_string(),\n79\t        session_id: SESSION.to_string(),\n80\t        ulid: stable_ulid(seed),\n81\t    }\n82\t}\n83\t\n84\tpub(super) fn memory_identity(seed: &str) -> MemoryId {\n85\t    MemoryId {\n86\t        workspace_id: WORKSPACE.to_string(),\n87\t        ulid: stable_ulid(seed),\n88\t    }\n89\t}\n90\t\n91\tpub(super) fn stable_ulid(seed: &str) -> String {\n92\t    const ALPHABET: &[u8; 32] = b\"0123456789ABCDEFGHJKMNPQRSTVWXYZ\";\n93\t    let mut bytes = [b'0'; 26];\n94\t    bytes[..24].copy_from_slice(b\"01ARZ3NDEKTSV4RRFFQ69G5F\");\n95\t    let checksum = seed.bytes().fold(0_u32, |acc, byte| {\n96\t        acc.wrapping_mul(33).wrapping_add(u32::from(byte))\n97\t    });\n98\t    bytes[24] = ALPHABET[((checksum >> 5) & 31) as usize];\n99\t    bytes[25] = ALPHABET[(checksum & 31) as usize];\n100\t    String::from_utf8(bytes.to_vec()).expect(\"stable ULID is valid ASCII\")\n101\t}\n102\t\n103\tpub(super) fn branch_scope_state() -> MemoryScopeState {\n104\t    MemoryScopeState {\n105\t        scope: MemoryScope::Branch,\n106\t        scope_session_id: None,\n107\t        scope_branch: Some(BRANCH.to_string()),\n108\t        scope_workspace_id: Some(WORKSPACE.to_string()),\n109\t        scope_user_id: None,\n110\t        scope_org_id: None,\n111\t    }\n112\t}\n113\t\n114\tpub(super) fn idem(value: &str) -> IdempotencyKey {\n115\t    IdempotencyKey::new(value.to_string()).expect(\"idempotency key\")\n116\t}\n117\t\n118\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n119\t// In-process collaborator harness\n120\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n121\t\n122\t/// Wiring that mirrors `memory_graph::tests_common::TestHarness` but lives\n123\t/// inside `contract_tests` so the cross-layer surface is exercised without\n124\t/// re-exporting a private per-substrate helper.\n125\tpub(super) struct ContractHarness {\n126\t    _tempdir: TempDir,\n127\t    pub(super) conn: Arc<Mutex<Connection>>,\n128\t    pub(super) event_store: Arc<EventStore>,\n129\t    pub(super) store: MemoryStore,\n130\t}\n131\t\n132\timpl ContractHarness {\n133\t    pub(super) fn new() -> Self {\n134\t        let tempdir = TempDir::new().expect(\"contract tempdir\");\n135\t        let conn = Connection::open(tempdir.path().join(\"memory-graph.db\"))\n136\t            .expect(\"memory graph DB opens\");\n137\t        conn.execute_batch(\"PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON;\")\n138\t            .expect(\"foreign keys enable\");\n139\t        initialize_schema(&conn).expect(\"memory graph schema initializes\");\n140\t        let conn = Arc::new(Mutex::new(conn));\n141\t        let event_store = Arc::new(\n142\t            EventStore::open(&tempdir.path().join(\"events.db\")).expect(\"event store opens\"),\n143\t        );\n144\t        let writer = Arc::new(\n145\t            EventWriter::new(event_store.clone(), WORKSPACE.to_string(), 4096)\n146\t                .with_flush_policy(FlushPolicy::Sync),\n147\t        );\n148\t        let store = MemoryStore::open(conn.clone(), writer);\n149\t        Self {\n150\t            _tempdir: tempdir,\n151\t            conn,\n152\t            event_store,\n153\t            store,\n154\t        }\n155\t    }\n156\t\n157\t    pub(super) fn conn(&self) -> std::sync::MutexGuard<'_, Connection> {\n158\t        self.conn.lock().expect(\"contract harness DB lock\")\n159\t    }\n160\t\n161\t    pub(super) fn writer(&self) -> EventWriter {\n162\t        EventWriter::new(self.event_store.clone(), WORKSPACE.to_string(), 4096)\n163\t            .with_flush_policy(FlushPolicy::Sync)\n164\t    }\n165\t\n166\t    pub(super) fn reader(&self) -> EventReader {\n167\t        EventReader::new(self.event_store.clone())\n168\t    }\n169\t\n170\t    pub(super) fn all_memory_events(&self) -> Vec<EventEnvelope> {\n171\t        self.reader()\n172\t            .execute(\n173\t                EventQuery::new()\n174\t                    .session(\"memory-graph\")\n175\t                    .workspace(WORKSPACE)\n176\t                    .branch(BRANCH)\n177\t                    .order(QueryOrder::OldestFirst)\n178\t                    .limit(200),\n179\t            )\n180\t            .expect(\"memory graph events load\")\n181\t    }\n182\t}\n183\t\n184\tpub(super) fn append_event(writer: &EventWriter, partial: PartialEnvelope) -> EventId {\n185\t    writer.append(partial).expect(\"event appends\")\n186\t}\n187\t\n188\t/// Convenience constructor for the workspace/branch/session-scoped envelopes\n189\t/// every cross-layer test in this gate uses. Surfaces stay readable when the\n190\t/// test body shows only the kind, references, and typed payload that\n191\t/// distinguish it.\n192\tpub(super) fn daemon_envelope(\n193\t    kind: crate::events::EventKind,\n194\t    references: Vec<crate::events::StableRef>,\n195\t    summary: &str,\n196\t    payload: crate::events::EventPayload,\n197\t) -> PartialEnvelope {\n198\t    PartialEnvelope {\n199\t        workspace_id: Some(WORKSPACE.to_string()),\n200\t        branch: crate::events::BranchRef {\n201\t            name: BRANCH.to_string(),\n202\t        },\n203\t        session_id: crate::events::SessionId {\n204\t            value: SESSION.to_string(),\n205\t        },\n206\t        task_id: None,\n207\t        actor: Actor::Daemon,\n208\t        kind,\n209\t        references,\n210\t        summary: crate::events::CompactSummary::new(summary.to_string())\n211\t            .expect(\"contract summary fits\"),\n212\t        payload,\n213\t    }\n214\t}\n215\t\n216\tpub(super) fn read_back(reader: &EventReader, event_id: &EventId) -> EventEnvelope {\n217\t    let envelopes = reader\n218\t        .execute(\n219\t            EventQuery::new()\n220\t                .workspace(WORKSPACE)\n221\t                .branch(BRANCH)\n222\t                .order(QueryOrder::OldestFirst)\n223\t                .limit(100),\n224\t        )\n225\t        .expect(\"workspace-scoped read succeeds\");\n226\t    envelopes\n227\t        .into_iter()\n228\t        .find(|envelope| envelope.event_id == *event_id)\n229\t        .expect(\"appended event is visible to the reader\")\n230\t}\n231\t\n232\tpub(super) fn seed_draft(file: &FileId, symbol: &SymbolId, section: &SectionId) -> MemoryDraft {\n233\t    MemoryDraft {\n234\t        content: \"round-trip seed\".to_string(),\n235\t        class: MemoryClass::Observation,\n236\t        assertion_type: AssertionType::Observation,\n237\t        scope: branch_scope_state(),\n238\t        confidence: 0.8,\n239\t        confidence_reason: \"contract seed\".to_string(),\n240\t        freshness_policy: FreshnessPolicy {\n241\t            kind: FreshnessKind::BranchScoped,\n242\t            ttl: None,\n243\t            recheck_interval: None,\n244\t        },\n245\t        validity_conditions: Vec::new(),\n246\t        invalidation_triggers: Vec::new(),\n247\t        provenance_event_ids: Vec::new(),\n248\t        evidence_references: Vec::new(),\n249\t        linked_files: vec![file.clone()],\n250\t        linked_symbols: vec![symbol.clone()],\n251\t        linked_docs: vec![section.clone()],\n252\t        linked_tests: Vec::new(),\n253\t        linked_memories: Vec::new(),\n254\t        contradiction_links: Vec::new(),\n255\t        supersession_links: Vec::new(),\n256\t        access_history: Vec::new(),\n257\t        created_by: \"assistant\".to_string(),\n258\t        updated_by: \"assistant\".to_string(),\n259\t        superseded_by: None,\n260\t        schema_version: 1,\n261\t        initial_evidence: vec![file_span_evidence(file)],\n262\t    }\n263\t}\n264\t\n265\tpub(super) fn file_span_evidence(file: &FileId) -> MemoryEvidence {\n266\t    MemoryEvidence {\n267\t        evidence_id: MemoryEvidenceId(String::new()),\n268\t        memory_id: memory_identity(\"placeholder\"),\n269\t        event_id: None,\n270\t        anchor: EvidenceAnchor::FileSpan {\n271\t            file: file.clone(),\n272\t            byte_start: 0,\n273\t            byte_end: 32,\n274\t            sha256: [0_u8; 32],\n275\t        },\n276\t        captured_at: DateTime::from_unix_seconds(1_700_000_000),\n277\t        captured_by: Actor::Daemon,\n278\t    }\n279\t}\n280\t\n281\tpub(super) fn doc_section_evidence(section: &SectionId) -> MemoryEvidence {\n282\t    MemoryEvidence {\n283\t        evidence_id: MemoryEvidenceId(String::new()),\n284\t        memory_id: memory_identity(\"placeholder\"),\n285\t        event_id: None,\n286\t        anchor: EvidenceAnchor::DocSection {\n287\t            id: section.clone(),\n288\t            sha256: [1_u8; 32],\n289\t        },\n290\t        captured_at: DateTime::from_unix_seconds(1_700_000_010),\n291\t        captured_by: Actor::Daemon,\n292\t    }\n293\t}\n294\t\n295\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n296\t// Legacy memory source used by the migration round-trip tests.\n297\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n298\t\n299\tpub(super) fn legacy_source_conn() -> Connection {\n300\t    let conn = Connection::open_in_memory().expect(\"legacy source DB\");\n301\t    conn.execute_batch(\n302\t        \"CREATE TABLE memories (\n303\t            id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n304\t            session_id TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '',\n305\t            content TEXT NOT NULL,\n306\t            memory_type TEXT NOT NULL,\n307\t            scope TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'session',\n308\t            confidence REAL NOT NULL DEFAULT 1.0,\n309\t            linked_symbols TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '[]',\n310\t            linked_files TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '[]',\n311\t            workspace_id TEXT,\n312\t            branch TEXT,\n313\t            refresh_key TEXT,\n314\t            source_query TEXT,\n315\t            assertion_type TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'observation',\n316\t            verification_status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'unverified',\n317\t            confidence_reason TEXT,\n318\t            supersedes_memory_id TEXT,\n319\t            superseded_by_memory_id TEXT,\n320\t            contradicts_memory_ids TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '[]',\n321\t            contradicted_by_memory_ids TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '[]',\n322\t            freshness_policy TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'session_scoped',\n323\t            freshness_policy_detail TEXT,\n324\t            provenance_json TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '[]',\n325\t            evidence_json TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '[]',\n326\t            created_at INTEGER NOT NULL,\n327\t            last_accessed INTEGER NOT NULL,\n328\t            access_count INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n329\t            is_stale INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n330\t            stale_reason TEXT,\n331\t            is_invalidated INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0\n332\t        );\",\n333\t    )\n334\t    .expect(\"legacy schema\");\n335\t    conn\n336\t}\n337\t\n338\tpub(super) fn insert_legacy_row(conn: &Connection, id: &str, linked_files_json: &str) {\n339\t    conn.execute(\n340\t        \"INSERT INTO memories\n341\t            (id, session_id, content, memory_type, scope, confidence, linked_symbols,\n342\t             linked_files, workspace_id, branch, refresh_key, source_query, assertion_type,\n343\t             verification_status, confidence_reason, supersedes_memory_id,\n344\t             superseded_by_memory_id, contradicts_memory_ids, contradicted_by_memory_ids,\n345\t             freshness_policy, freshness_policy_detail, provenance_json, evidence_json,\n346\t             created_at, last_accessed, access_count, is_stale, stale_reason, is_invalidated)\n347\t         VALUES\n348\t            (?1, 'legacy-session', ?2, 'observation', 'repo', 0.7, '[]', ?3, ?4, 'main',\n349\t             NULL, NULL, 'observation', 'unverified', NULL, NULL, NULL,\n350\t             '[]', '[]', 'repo_scoped', NULL, '[]', '[]', 1700000000, 1700000000, 0, 0, NULL, 0)\",\n351\t        rusqlite::params![id, format!(\"memory {id}\"), linked_files_json, WORKSPACE],\n352\t    )\n353\t    .expect(\"legacy row inserts\");\n354\t}\n355\t\n356\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n357\t// Resolver fixture builders for the rename and end-to-end round-trip tests.\n358\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n359\t\n360\tpub(super) fn build_empty_resolver(\n361\t    workspace: &str,\n362\t    events: Vec<EventId>,\n363\t) -> IdentityResolver<'static> {\n364\t    let graph = Box::leak(Box::new(CodeGraph::new()));\n365\t    let file_index: HashMap<String, FileIndexEntry> = HashMap::new();\n366\t    let parsed_files: HashMap<String, crate::symbols::ParsedFile> = HashMap::new();\n367\t    IdentityResolver::new(\n368\t        graph,\n369\t        Box::leak(Box::new(file_index)),\n370\t        Box::leak(Box::new(parsed_files)),\n371\t        workspace.to_string(),\n372\t        events,\n373\t    )\n374\t}\n375\t\n376\tpub(super) fn build_filesystem_resolver(\n377\t    default_workspace: &str,\n378\t    files: &[(&str, &str, &str)],\n379\t) -> IdentityResolver<'static> {\n380\t    let mut graph = CodeGraph::new();\n381\t    let mut file_index: HashMap<String, FileIndexEntry> = HashMap::new();\n382\t    let mut parsed_files: HashMap<String, crate::symbols::ParsedFile> = HashMap::new();\n383\t    for (workspace, path, source) in files.iter() {\n384\t        let stored_path = format!(\"{}/{}\", workspace, path);\n385\t        let parsed = parse_file(&stored_path, source).expect(\"fixture parses\");\n386\t        for symbol in &parsed.symbols {\n387\t            graph.add_node(\n388\t                symbol.id.clone(),\n389\t                symbol.kind,\n390\t                symbol.name.clone(),\n391\t                symbol.signature.clone(),\n392\t                symbol.body.clone(),\n393\t                symbol.file.clone(),\n394\t                symbol.line,\n395\t                symbol.end_line,\n396\t                symbol.is_exported,\n397\t                symbol.language,\n398\t            );\n399\t        }\n400\t        parsed_files.insert(stored_path.clone(), parsed);\n401\t        file_index.insert(\n402\t            stored_path.clone(),\n403\t            FileIndexEntry {\n404\t                file: stored_path.clone(),\n405\t                content_hash: deterministic_hash(source),\n406\t                mtime_ns: 0,\n407\t                size_bytes: source.len() as i64,\n408\t                parser_version: FILE_INDEX_PARSER_VERSION,\n409\t                schema_version: FILE_INDEX_SCHEMA_VERSION,\n410\t                last_indexed_at: 0,\n411\t            },\n412\t        );\n413\t    }\n414\t    IdentityResolver::new(\n415\t        Box::leak(Box::new(graph)),\n416\t        Box::leak(Box::new(file_index)),\n417\t        Box::leak(Box::new(parsed_files)),\n418\t        default_workspace.to_string(),\n419\t        Vec::new(),\n420\t    )\n421\t}\n422\t\n423\tfn deterministic_hash(source: &str) -> String {\n424\t    let mut hash = 0xcbf29ce484222325u64;\n425\t    for byte in source.as_bytes() {\n426\t        hash ^= *byte as u64;\n427\t        hash = hash.wrapping_mul(0x100000001b3);\n428\t    }\n429\t    format!(\"{hash:016x}\")\n430\t}\n431\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"623701ab-dc49-4054-96ef-292da32369e2","uuid":"0e8882eb-7434-43d0-9ef0-5399862e7068","timestamp":"2026-05-17T13:09:15.387Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/contract_tests/identity_event_memory_support.rs","content":"//! Shared fixtures, harness, and identity factories for the R26 cross-layer\n//! contract tests in `identity_event_memory.rs`.\n//!\n//! These helpers exist so the test file can stay focused on the contract\n//! surfaces it pins. Per the Cadres coding standard `## Hard limits`, this\n//! support module keeps the test file under the 800-line ceiling without\n//! losing the per-surface organization that makes the gate readable.\n\nuse std::collections::HashMap;\nuse std::sync::{Arc, Mutex};\n\nuse rusqlite::Connection;\nuse tempfile::TempDir;\n\nuse crate::events::{\n    Actor, EventEnvelope, EventQuery, EventReader, EventStore, EventWriter, FlushPolicy,\n    PartialEnvelope, QueryOrder,\n};\nuse crate::graph::CodeGraph;\nuse crate::identity::{\n    ContextHandleId, DocId, EventId, FileId, IdentityResolver, MemoryId, SectionId, SymbolId,\n};\nuse crate::memory_graph::store::MemoryScopeState;\nuse crate::memory_graph::{\n    initialize_schema, AssertionType, EvidenceAnchor, FreshnessKind, FreshnessPolicy,\n    IdempotencyKey, MemoryClass, MemoryDraft, MemoryEvidence, MemoryEvidenceId, MemoryScope,\n    MemoryStore,\n};\nuse crate::parser::parse_file;\nuse crate::storage::graph_store::{\n    FileIndexEntry, FILE_INDEX_PARSER_VERSION, FILE_INDEX_SCHEMA_VERSION,\n};\nuse crate::DateTime;\n\npub(super) const WORKSPACE: &str = \"workspace\";\npub(super) const BRANCH: &str = \"main\";\npub(super) const SESSION: &str = \"contract-session\";\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Identity factories\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\npub(super) fn file_identity(path: &str) -> FileId {\n    FileId {\n        workspace_id: WORKSPACE.to_string(),\n        repo_relative_path: path.to_string(),\n        content_hash: \"feedface00000001\".to_string(),\n    }\n}\n\npub(super) fn doc_identity(path: &str) -> DocId {\n    DocId {\n        workspace_id: WORKSPACE.to_string(),\n        repo_relative_path: path.to_string(),\n        content_hash: \"deadbeef00000002\".to_string(),\n    }\n}\n\npub(super) fn section_identity(path: &str, heading: &str) -> SectionId {\n    SectionId {\n        doc: doc_identity(path),\n        heading_path: vec![heading.to_string()],\n        byte_offset: 64,\n    }\n}\n\npub(super) fn symbol_identity(file: &FileId, qualified: &str) -> SymbolId {\n    SymbolId {\n        file: file.clone(),\n        qualified_name: qualified.to_string(),\n        byte_offset: 12,\n        kind: \"function\".to_string(),\n    }\n}\n\npub(super) fn context_handle_identity(seed: &str) -> ContextHandleId {\n    ContextHandleId {\n        workspace_id: WORKSPACE.to_string(),\n        session_id: SESSION.to_string(),\n        ulid: stable_ulid(seed),\n    }\n}\n\npub(super) fn memory_identity(seed: &str) -> MemoryId {\n    MemoryId {\n        workspace_id: WORKSPACE.to_string(),\n        ulid: stable_ulid(seed),\n    }\n}\n\npub(super) fn stable_ulid(seed: &str) -> String {\n    const ALPHABET: &[u8; 32] = b\"0123456789ABCDEFGHJKMNPQRSTVWXYZ\";\n    let mut bytes = [b'0'; 26];\n    bytes[..24].copy_from_slice(b\"01ARZ3NDEKTSV4RRFFQ69G5F\");\n    let checksum = seed.bytes().fold(0_u32, |acc, byte| {\n        acc.wrapping_mul(33).wrapping_add(u32::from(byte))\n    });\n    bytes[24] = ALPHABET[((checksum >> 5) & 31) as usize];\n    bytes[25] = ALPHABET[(checksum & 31) as usize];\n    String::from_utf8(bytes.to_vec()).expect(\"stable ULID is valid ASCII\")\n}\n\npub(super) fn branch_scope_state() -> MemoryScopeState {\n    MemoryScopeState {\n        scope: MemoryScope::Branch,\n        scope_session_id: None,\n        scope_branch: Some(BRANCH.to_string()),\n        scope_workspace_id: Some(WORKSPACE.to_string()),\n        scope_user_id: None,\n        scope_org_id: None,\n    }\n}\n\npub(super) fn idem(value: &str) -> IdempotencyKey {\n    IdempotencyKey::new(value.to_string()).expect(\"idempotency key\")\n}\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// In-process collaborator harness\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n/// Wiring that mirrors `memory_graph::tests_common::TestHarness` but lives\n/// inside `contract_tests` so the cross-layer surface is exercised without\n/// re-exporting a private per-substrate helper.\npub(super) struct ContractHarness {\n    _tempdir: TempDir,\n    pub(super) conn: Arc<Mutex<Connection>>,\n    pub(super) event_store: Arc<EventStore>,\n    pub(super) store: MemoryStore,\n}\n\nimpl ContractHarness {\n    pub(super) fn new() -> Self {\n        let tempdir = TempDir::new().expect(\"contract tempdir\");\n        let conn = Connection::open(tempdir.path().join(\"memory-graph.db\"))\n            .expect(\"memory graph DB opens\");\n        conn.execute_batch(\"PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON;\")\n            .expect(\"foreign keys enable\");\n        initialize_schema(&conn).expect(\"memory graph schema initializes\");\n        let conn = Arc::new(Mutex::new(conn));\n        let event_store = Arc::new(\n            EventStore::open(&tempdir.path().join(\"events.db\")).expect(\"event store opens\"),\n        );\n        let writer = Arc::new(\n            EventWriter::new(event_store.clone(), WORKSPACE.to_string(), 4096)\n                .with_flush_policy(FlushPolicy::Sync),\n        );\n        let store = MemoryStore::open(conn.clone(), writer);\n        Self {\n            _tempdir: tempdir,\n            conn,\n            event_store,\n            store,\n        }\n    }\n\n    pub(super) fn conn(&self) -> std::sync::MutexGuard<'_, Connection> {\n        self.conn.lock().expect(\"contract harness DB lock\")\n    }\n\n    pub(super) fn writer(&self) -> EventWriter {\n        EventWriter::new(self.event_store.clone(), WORKSPACE.to_string(), 4096)\n            .with_flush_policy(FlushPolicy::Sync)\n    }\n\n    pub(super) fn reader(&self) -> EventReader {\n        EventReader::new(self.event_store.clone())\n    }\n\n    pub(super) fn all_memory_events(&self) -> Vec<EventEnvelope> {\n        self.reader()\n            .execute(\n                EventQuery::new()\n                    .session(\"memory-graph\")\n                    .workspace(WORKSPACE)\n                    .branch(BRANCH)\n                    .order(QueryOrder::OldestFirst)\n                    .limit(200),\n            )\n            .expect(\"memory graph events load\")\n    }\n}\n\npub(super) fn append_event(writer: &EventWriter, partial: PartialEnvelope) -> EventId {\n    writer.append(partial).expect(\"event appends\")\n}\n\n/// Convenience constructor for the workspace/branch/session-scoped envelopes\n/// every cross-layer test in this gate uses. Surfaces stay readable when the\n/// test body shows only the kind, references, and typed payload that\n/// distinguish it.\npub(super) fn daemon_envelope(\n    kind: crate::events::EventKind,\n    references: Vec<crate::events::StableRef>,\n    summary: &str,\n    payload: crate::events::EventPayload,\n) -> PartialEnvelope {\n    PartialEnvelope {\n        workspace_id: Some(WORKSPACE.to_string()),\n        branch: crate::events::BranchRef {\n            name: BRANCH.to_string(),\n        },\n        session_id: crate::events::SessionId {\n            value: SESSION.to_string(),\n        },\n        task_id: None,\n        actor: Actor::Daemon,\n        kind,\n        references,\n        summary: crate::events::CompactSummary::new(summary.to_string())\n            .expect(\"contract summary fits\"),\n        payload,\n    }\n}\n\npub(super) fn read_back(reader: &EventReader, event_id: &EventId) -> EventEnvelope {\n    let envelopes = reader\n        .execute(\n            EventQuery::new()\n                .workspace(WORKSPACE)\n                .branch(BRANCH)\n                .order(QueryOrder::OldestFirst)\n                .limit(100),\n        )\n        .expect(\"workspace-scoped read succeeds\");\n    envelopes\n        .into_iter()\n        .find(|envelope| envelope.event_id == *event_id)\n        .expect(\"appended event is visible to the reader\")\n}\n\npub(super) fn seed_draft(file: &FileId, symbol: &SymbolId, section: &SectionId) -> MemoryDraft {\n    MemoryDraft {\n        content: \"round-trip seed\".to_string(),\n        class: MemoryClass::Observation,\n        assertion_type: AssertionType::Observation,\n        scope: branch_scope_state(),\n        confidence: 0.8,\n        confidence_reason: \"contract seed\".to_string(),\n        freshness_policy: FreshnessPolicy {\n            kind: FreshnessKind::BranchScoped,\n            ttl: None,\n            recheck_interval: None,\n        },\n        validity_conditions: Vec::new(),\n        invalidation_triggers: Vec::new(),\n        provenance_event_ids: Vec::new(),\n        evidence_references: Vec::new(),\n        linked_files: vec![file.clone()],\n        linked_symbols: vec![symbol.clone()],\n        linked_docs: vec![section.clone()],\n        linked_tests: Vec::new(),\n        linked_memories: Vec::new(),\n        contradiction_links: Vec::new(),\n        supersession_links: Vec::new(),\n        access_history: Vec::new(),\n        created_by: \"assistant\".to_string(),\n        updated_by: \"assistant\".to_string(),\n        superseded_by: None,\n        schema_version: 1,\n        initial_evidence: vec![file_span_evidence(file)],\n    }\n}\n\npub(super) fn file_span_evidence(file: &FileId) -> MemoryEvidence {\n    MemoryEvidence {\n        evidence_id: MemoryEvidenceId(String::new()),\n        memory_id: memory_identity(\"placeholder\"),\n        event_id: None,\n        anchor: EvidenceAnchor::FileSpan {\n            file: file.clone(),\n            byte_start: 0,\n            byte_end: 32,\n            sha256: [0_u8; 32],\n        },\n        captured_at: DateTime::from_unix_seconds(1_700_000_000),\n        captured_by: Actor::Daemon,\n    }\n}\n\npub(super) fn doc_section_evidence(section: &SectionId) -> MemoryEvidence {\n    MemoryEvidence {\n        evidence_id: MemoryEvidenceId(String::new()),\n        memory_id: memory_identity(\"placeholder\"),\n        event_id: None,\n        anchor: EvidenceAnchor::DocSection {\n            id: section.clone(),\n            sha256: [1_u8; 32],\n        },\n        captured_at: DateTime::from_unix_seconds(1_700_000_010),\n        captured_by: Actor::Daemon,\n    }\n}\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Legacy memory source used by the migration round-trip tests.\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\npub(super) fn legacy_source_conn() -> Connection {\n    let conn = Connection::open_in_memory().expect(\"legacy source DB\");\n    conn.execute_batch(\n        \"CREATE TABLE memories (\n            id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n            session_id TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '',\n            content TEXT NOT NULL,\n            memory_type TEXT NOT NULL,\n            scope TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'session',\n            confidence REAL NOT NULL DEFAULT 1.0,\n            linked_symbols TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '[]',\n            linked_files TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '[]',\n            workspace_id TEXT,\n            branch TEXT,\n            refresh_key TEXT,\n            source_query TEXT,\n            assertion_type TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'observation',\n            verification_status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'unverified',\n            confidence_reason TEXT,\n            supersedes_memory_id TEXT,\n            superseded_by_memory_id TEXT,\n            contradicts_memory_ids TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '[]',\n            contradicted_by_memory_ids TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '[]',\n            freshness_policy TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'session_scoped',\n            freshness_policy_detail TEXT,\n            provenance_json TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '[]',\n            evidence_json TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '[]',\n            created_at INTEGER NOT NULL,\n            last_accessed INTEGER NOT NULL,\n            access_count INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n            is_stale INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n            stale_reason TEXT,\n            is_invalidated INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0\n        );\",\n    )\n    .expect(\"legacy schema\");\n    conn\n}\n\npub(super) fn insert_legacy_row(conn: &Connection, id: &str, linked_files_json: &str) {\n    conn.execute(\n        \"INSERT INTO memories\n            (id, session_id, content, memory_type, scope, confidence, linked_symbols,\n             linked_files, workspace_id, branch, refresh_key, source_query, assertion_type,\n             verification_status, confidence_reason, supersedes_memory_id,\n             superseded_by_memory_id, contradicts_memory_ids, contradicted_by_memory_ids,\n             freshness_policy, freshness_policy_detail, provenance_json, evidence_json,\n             created_at, last_accessed, access_count, is_stale, stale_reason, is_invalidated)\n         VALUES\n            (?1, 'legacy-session', ?2, 'observation', 'repo', 0.7, '[]', ?3, ?4, 'main',\n             NULL, NULL, 'observation', 'unverified', NULL, NULL, NULL,\n             '[]', '[]', 'repo_scoped', NULL, '[]', '[]', 1700000000, 1700000000, 0, 0, NULL, 0)\",\n        rusqlite::params![id, format!(\"memory {id}\"), linked_files_json, WORKSPACE],\n    )\n    .expect(\"legacy row inserts\");\n}\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Resolver fixture builders for the rename and end-to-end round-trip tests.\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\npub(super) fn build_empty_resolver(\n    workspace: &str,\n    events: Vec<EventId>,\n) -> IdentityResolver<'static> {\n    let graph = Box::leak(Box::new(CodeGraph::new()));\n    let file_index: HashMap<String, FileIndexEntry> = HashMap::new();\n    let parsed_files: HashMap<String, crate::symbols::ParsedFile> = HashMap::new();\n    IdentityResolver::new(\n        graph,\n        Box::leak(Box::new(file_index)),\n        Box::leak(Box::new(parsed_files)),\n        workspace.to_string(),\n        events,\n    )\n}\n\npub(super) fn build_filesystem_resolver(\n    default_workspace: &str,\n    files: &[(&str, &str, &str)],\n) -> IdentityResolver<'static> {\n    let mut graph = CodeGraph::new();\n    let mut file_index: HashMap<String, FileIndexEntry> = HashMap::new();\n    let mut parsed_files: HashMap<String, crate::symbols::ParsedFile> = HashMap::new();\n    for (workspace, path, source) in files.iter() {\n        let stored_path = format!(\"{}/{}\", workspace, path);\n        let parsed = parse_file(&stored_path, source).expect(\"fixture parses\");\n        for symbol in &parsed.symbols {\n            graph.add_node(\n                symbol.id.clone(),\n                symbol.kind,\n                symbol.name.clone(),\n                symbol.signature.clone(),\n                symbol.body.clone(),\n                symbol.file.clone(),\n                symbol.line,\n                symbol.end_line,\n                symbol.is_exported,\n                symbol.language,\n            );\n        }\n        parsed_files.insert(stored_path.clone(), parsed);\n        file_index.insert(\n            stored_path.clone(),\n            FileIndexEntry {\n                file: stored_path.clone(),\n                content_hash: deterministic_hash(source),\n                mtime_ns: 0,\n                size_bytes: source.len() as i64,\n                parser_version: FILE_INDEX_PARSER_VERSION,\n                schema_version: FILE_INDEX_SCHEMA_VERSION,\n                last_indexed_at: 0,\n            },\n        );\n    }\n    IdentityResolver::new(\n        Box::leak(Box::new(graph)),\n        Box::leak(Box::new(file_index)),\n        Box::leak(Box::new(parsed_files)),\n        default_workspace.to_string(),\n        Vec::new(),\n    )\n}\n\nfn deterministic_hash(source: &str) -> String {\n    let mut hash = 0xcbf29ce484222325u64;\n    for byte in source.as_bytes() {\n        hash ^= *byte as u64;\n        hash = hash.wrapping_mul(0x100000001b3);\n    }\n    format!(\"{hash:016x}\")\n}\n","numLines":431,"startLine":1,"totalLines":431}}}
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/R55.log:29:{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SSCgUQSQWjVHYRWnasv4UG","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t//! Verification engine core for durable memory evidence.\n2\t//!\n3\t//! This module implements the verifier contract from\n4\t//! `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md`\n5\t//! `## 8. Verification Engine`,\n6\t//! `## Phase 7: Verification And Freshness`, and\n7\t//! `## Storage Design`.\n8\t//!\n9\t//! Verification checks:\n10\t//!\n11\t//! - linked files still exist\n12\t//! - linked symbols still exist\n13\t//! - cited docs still exist\n14\t//! - linked tests still exist\n15\t//! - evidence text still matches when exact spans were captured\n16\t//! - implementation still matches memory claim where deterministic checks are possible\n17\t//! - contradicted/superseded states remain coherent\n18\t//! - branch-scoped memory is not leaking into unrelated branches\n19\t//! - time-bound memory has expired\n20\t//!\n21\t//! Verification outputs:\n22\t//!\n23\t//! - `verified`\n24\t//! - `unverified`\n25\t//! - `in_review`\n26\t//! - `stale`\n27\t//! - `contradicted`\n28\t//! - `superseded`\n29\t//! - `expired`\n30\t//! - `invalidated`\n31\t\n32\tuse std::fmt;\n33\tuse std::str::FromStr;\n34\t\n35\tuse rusqlite::Connection;\n36\tuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\n37\t\n38\tuse crate::error::LatticeError;\n39\t\n40\tpub mod existence;\n41\tpub mod expiry;\n42\tpub mod incremental;\n43\tpub mod scope_enforcement;\n44\tpub mod spans;\n45\tpub mod surfacing;\n46\t\n47\t#[cfg(test)]\n48\tmod existence_tests;\n49\t#[cfg(test)]\n50\tmod incremental_tests;\n51\t#[cfg(test)]\n52\tmod integration_tests;\n53\t#[cfg(test)]\n54\tmod scope_leak_tests;\n55\t#[cfg(test)]\n56\tmod spans_tests;\n57\t#[cfg(test)]\n58\tmod surfacing_tests;\n59\t\n60\tpub use existence::{\n61\t    VerificationError, VerificationOutcome, VerifierBudget, VerifierCore, VerifierReport,\n62\t};\n63\tpub use expiry::{ExpiryError, ExpiryReport, ExpiryScanner};\n64\tpub use incremental::{\n65\t    IncrementalError, IncrementalReport, IncrementalVerifier, VerificationObserver,\n66\t};\n67\tpub use scope_enforcement::{\n68\t    allows, MemoryScopeFilteredEvent, OrganizationId, ScopeEnforcement, ScopeFilter,\n69\t    ScopeFilterError,\n70\t};\n71\tpub use spans::{\n72\t    SpanMismatch, SpanMismatchReason, SpanReader, SpanValidationError, SpanValidator,\n73\t    WorkspaceFileReader,\n74\t};\n75\tpub use surfacing::{\n76\t    classify_status, BundleProducer, BundleSection, LabeledMemory, SurfacedBundle, SurfacingError,\n77\t    SurfacingPipeline,\n78\t};\n79\t\n80\tconst VERIFICATION_SCHEMA_SQL: &str = include_str!(\"schema.sql\");\n81\t\n82\tpub fn initialize_schema(conn: &Connection) -> Result<(), LatticeError> {\n83\t    conn.execute_batch(VERIFICATION_SCHEMA_SQL)\n84\t        .map_err(|error| {\n85\t            LatticeError::Storage(format!(\"Failed to initialize verification schema: {error}\"))\n86\t        })?;\n87\t    Ok(())\n88\t}\n89\t\n90\t#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\n91\t#[serde(rename_all = \"snake_case\")]\n92\tpub enum VerificationStatus {\n93\t    Verified,\n94\t    Unverified,\n95\t    InReview,\n96\t    Stale,\n97\t    Contradicted,\n98\t    Superseded,\n99\t    Expired,\n100\t    Invalidated,\n101\t}\n102\t\n103\timpl VerificationStatus {\n104\t    pub const VALUES: &'static [&'static str] = &[\n105\t        \"verified\",\n106\t        \"unverified\",\n107\t        \"in_review\",\n108\t        \"stale\",\n109\t        \"contradicted\",\n110\t        \"superseded\",\n111\t        \"expired\",\n112\t        \"invalidated\",\n113\t    ];\n114\t\n115\t    pub fn as_str(self) -> &'static str {\n116\t        match self {\n117\t            Self::Verified => \"verified\",\n118\t            Self::Unverified => \"unverified\",\n119\t            Self::InReview => \"in_review\",\n120\t            Self::Stale => \"stale\",\n121\t            Self::Contradicted => \"contradicted\",\n122\t            Self::Superseded => \"superseded\",\n123\t            Self::Expired => \"expired\",\n124\t            Self::Invalidated => \"invalidated\",\n125\t        }\n126\t    }\n127\t}\n128\t\n129\timpl fmt::Display for VerificationStatus {\n130\t    fn fmt(&self, formatter: &mut fmt::Formatter<'_>) -> fmt::Result {\n131\t        formatter.write_str(self.as_str())\n132\t    }\n133\t}\n134\t\n135\timpl FromStr for VerificationStatus {\n136\t    type Err = LatticeError;\n137\t\n138\t    fn from_str(value: &str) -> Result<Self, Self::Err> {\n139\t        match value {\n140\t            \"verified\" => Ok(Self::Verified),\n141\t            \"unverified\" => Ok(Self::Unverified),\n142\t            \"in_review\" => Ok(Self::InReview),\n143\t            \"stale\" => Ok(Self::Stale),\n144\t            \"contradicted\" => Ok(Self::Contradicted),\n145\t            \"superseded\" => Ok(Self::Superseded),\n146\t            \"expired\" => Ok(Self::Expired),\n147\t            \"invalidated\" => Ok(Self::Invalidated),\n148\t            other => Err(LatticeError::Storage(format!(\n149\t                \"Unknown verification status '{other}'\"\n150\t            ))),\n151\t        }\n152\t    }\n153\t}\n154\t\n155\t#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\n156\tpub struct VerificationVerdict {\n157\t    pub status: VerificationStatus,\n158\t    pub reason: String,\n159\t}\n160\t\n161\timpl VerificationVerdict {\n162\t    pub fn new(status: VerificationStatus, reason: impl Into<String>) -> Self {\n163\t        Self {\n164\t            status,\n165\t            reason: reason.into(),\n166\t        }\n167\t    }\n168\t}\n169\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"623701ab-dc49-4054-96ef-292da32369e2","uuid":"aac935ef-dae2-4705-b0f2-6c7cc022727a","timestamp":"2026-05-17T13:09:18.567Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/verification/mod.rs","content":"//! Verification engine core for durable memory evidence.\n//!\n//! This module implements the verifier contract from\n//! `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md`\n//! `## 8. Verification Engine`,\n//! `## Phase 7: Verification And Freshness`, and\n//! `## Storage Design`.\n//!\n//! Verification checks:\n//!\n//! - linked files still exist\n//! - linked symbols still exist\n//! - cited docs still exist\n//! - linked tests still exist\n//! - evidence text still matches when exact spans were captured\n//! - implementation still matches memory claim where deterministic checks are possible\n//! - contradicted/superseded states remain coherent\n//! - branch-scoped memory is not leaking into unrelated branches\n//! - time-bound memory has expired\n//!\n//! Verification outputs:\n//!\n//! - `verified`\n//! - `unverified`\n//! - `in_review`\n//! - `stale`\n//! - `contradicted`\n//! - `superseded`\n//! - `expired`\n//! - `invalidated`\n\nuse std::fmt;\nuse std::str::FromStr;\n\nuse rusqlite::Connection;\nuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\n\nuse crate::error::LatticeError;\n\npub mod existence;\npub mod expiry;\npub mod incremental;\npub mod scope_enforcement;\npub mod spans;\npub mod surfacing;\n\n#[cfg(test)]\nmod existence_tests;\n#[cfg(test)]\nmod incremental_tests;\n#[cfg(test)]\nmod integration_tests;\n#[cfg(test)]\nmod scope_leak_tests;\n#[cfg(test)]\nmod spans_tests;\n#[cfg(test)]\nmod surfacing_tests;\n\npub use existence::{\n    VerificationError, VerificationOutcome, VerifierBudget, VerifierCore, VerifierReport,\n};\npub use expiry::{ExpiryError, ExpiryReport, ExpiryScanner};\npub use incremental::{\n    IncrementalError, IncrementalReport, IncrementalVerifier, VerificationObserver,\n};\npub use scope_enforcement::{\n    allows, MemoryScopeFilteredEvent, OrganizationId, ScopeEnforcement, ScopeFilter,\n    ScopeFilterError,\n};\npub use spans::{\n    SpanMismatch, SpanMismatchReason, SpanReader, SpanValidationError, SpanValidator,\n    WorkspaceFileReader,\n};\npub use surfacing::{\n    classify_status, BundleProducer, BundleSection, LabeledMemory, SurfacedBundle, SurfacingError,\n    SurfacingPipeline,\n};\n\nconst VERIFICATION_SCHEMA_SQL: &str = include_str!(\"schema.sql\");\n\npub fn initialize_schema(conn: &Connection) -> Result<(), LatticeError> {\n    conn.execute_batch(VERIFICATION_SCHEMA_SQL)\n        .map_err(|error| {\n            LatticeError::Storage(format!(\"Failed to initialize verification schema: {error}\"))\n        })?;\n    Ok(())\n}\n\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\n#[serde(rename_all = \"snake_case\")]\npub enum VerificationStatus {\n    Verified,\n    Unverified,\n    InReview,\n    Stale,\n    Contradicted,\n    Superseded,\n    Expired,\n    Invalidated,\n}\n\nimpl VerificationStatus {\n    pub const VALUES: &'static [&'static str] = &[\n        \"verified\",\n        \"unverified\",\n        \"in_review\",\n        \"stale\",\n        \"contradicted\",\n        \"superseded\",\n        \"expired\",\n        \"invalidated\",\n    ];\n\n    pub fn as_str(self) -> &'static str {\n        match self {\n            Self::Verified => \"verified\",\n            Self::Unverified => \"unverified\",\n            Self::InReview => \"in_review\",\n            Self::Stale => \"stale\",\n            Self::Contradicted => \"contradicted\",\n            Self::Superseded => \"superseded\",\n            Self::Expired => \"expired\",\n            Self::Invalidated => \"invalidated\",\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nimpl fmt::Display for VerificationStatus {\n    fn fmt(&self, formatter: &mut fmt::Formatter<'_>) -> fmt::Result {\n        formatter.write_str(self.as_str())\n    }\n}\n\nimpl FromStr for VerificationStatus {\n    type Err = LatticeError;\n\n    fn from_str(value: &str) -> Result<Self, Self::Err> {\n        match value {\n            \"verified\" => Ok(Self::Verified),\n            \"unverified\" => Ok(Self::Unverified),\n            \"in_review\" => Ok(Self::InReview),\n            \"stale\" => Ok(Self::Stale),\n            \"contradicted\" => Ok(Self::Contradicted),\n            \"superseded\" => Ok(Self::Superseded),\n            \"expired\" => Ok(Self::Expired),\n            \"invalidated\" => Ok(Self::Invalidated),\n            other => Err(LatticeError::Storage(format!(\n                \"Unknown verification status '{other}'\"\n            ))),\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\npub struct VerificationVerdict {\n    pub status: VerificationStatus,\n    pub reason: String,\n}\n\nimpl VerificationVerdict {\n    pub fn new(status: VerificationStatus, reason: impl Into<String>) -> Self {\n        Self {\n            status,\n            reason: reason.into(),\n        }\n    }\n}\n","numLines":169,"startLine":1,"totalLines":169}}}
