docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/R55.log:65:{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014Hr9M4eZ3vLvtRCposHF3y","type":"tool_result","content":"89\t## Non-Negotiable Product Properties\n90\t\n91\t- Local-first by default.\n92\t- Deterministic identities for every file, symbol, doc section, event, and memory.\n93\t- Every durable memory has evidence.\n94\t- Every retrieved memory has an inclusion reason.\n95\t- Every stale or contradicted memory is surfaced as such, not hidden behind recency.\n96\t- Every workflow bundle is compact by default with deliberate expansion handles.\n97\t- Every background consolidation pass is recoverable, replayable, and observable.\n98\t- Every public MCP contract is documented and regression-tested.\n99\t- No silent broad workspace reads that bypass ignore rules or workspace boundaries.\n100\t- No unbounded graph traversal, payload growth, or event-log scans on hot paths.\n101\t\n102\t## System Architecture\n103\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"623701ab-dc49-4054-96ef-292da32369e2","uuid":"1cfcee4e-de45-408b-b3c9-af04911721c1","timestamp":"2026-05-17T13:10:03.215Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md","content":"## Non-Negotiable Product Properties\n\n- Local-first by default.\n- Deterministic identities for every file, symbol, doc section, event, and memory.\n- Every durable memory has evidence.\n- Every retrieved memory has an inclusion reason.\n- Every stale or contradicted memory is surfaced as such, not hidden behind recency.\n- Every workflow bundle is compact by default with deliberate expansion handles.\n- Every background consolidation pass is recoverable, replayable, and observable.\n- Every public MCP contract is documented and regression-tested.\n- No silent broad workspace reads that bypass ignore rules or workspace boundaries.\n- No unbounded graph traversal, payload growth, or event-log scans on hot paths.\n\n## System Architecture\n","numLines":15,"startLine":89,"totalLines":969}}}
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/R55.log:71:{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012cVgyzRqfm1wAJ1iu3Xg81","type":"tool_result","content":"354\t### 7. Retrieval Engine\n355\t\n356\tRetrieval must be task-aware and explainable.\n357\t\n358\tPipeline:\n359\t\n360\t1. Parse user task and classify intent.\n361\t2. Extract literal anchors: paths, symbols, errors, commands, APIs, config keys.\n362\t3. Resolve anchors into graph identities.\n363\t4. Retrieve graph candidates.\n364\t5. Retrieve memory candidates from typed streams.\n365\t6. Retrieve relevant event episodes.\n366\t7. Expand through bounded graph and memory neighborhoods.\n367\t8. Score candidates.\n368\t9. Deduplicate and compress.\n369\t10. Return a compact bundle with inclusion reasons and expansion handles.\n370\t\n371\tCandidate sources:\n372\t\n373\t- exact path/symbol lookup\n374\t- code graph traversal\n375\t- doc backlinks/outgoing links\n376\t- FTS\n377\t- embeddings\n378\t- event similarity\n379\t- memory links\n380\t- workflow similarity\n381\t- recent active working memory\n382\t\n383\tRanking signals:\n384\t\n385\t- task-type compatibility\n386\t- graph proximity to anchors\n387\t- exact identifier match\n388\t- semantic similarity\n389\t- verification status\n390\t- freshness\n391\t- scope\n392\t- evidence strength\n393\t- contradiction/supersession state\n394\t- past usefulness\n395\t- recent successful reuse\n396\t- user preference compatibility\n397\t- token cost\n398\t\n399\tThe ranker should expose scores and reasons in diagnostic mode. Compact mode should include only enough explanation for an assistant to trust the result.\n400\t\n401\t### 8. Verification Engine\n402\t\n403\tThe verification engine keeps memory honest.\n404\t\n405\tVerification checks:\n406\t\n407\t- linked files still exist\n408\t- linked symbols still exist\n409\t- cited docs still exist\n410\t- linked tests still exist\n411\t- evidence text still matches when exact spans were captured\n412\t- implementation still matches memory claim where deterministic checks are possible\n413\t- contradicted/superseded states remain coherent\n414\t- branch-scoped memory is not leaking into unrelated branches\n415\t- time-bound memory has expired\n416\t\n417\tVerification outputs:\n418\t\n419\t- `verified`\n420\t- `unverified`\n421\t- `in_review`\n422\t- `stale`\n423\t- `contradicted`\n424\t- `superseded`\n425\t- `expired`\n426\t- `invalidated`\n427\t\n428\tVerification must be incremental and tied to workspace changes. Large repos cannot tolerate full rescans for every memory.\n429\t\n430\t### 9. MCP Surface\n431\t\n432\tThe MCP contract should expose high-level assistant workflows rather than forcing clients to compose low-level graph calls.\n433\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"623701ab-dc49-4054-96ef-292da32369e2","uuid":"21bec931-aac0-4434-9336-8c49098b54e0","timestamp":"2026-05-17T13:10:12.327Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md","content":"### 7. Retrieval Engine\n\nRetrieval must be task-aware and explainable.\n\nPipeline:\n\n1. Parse user task and classify intent.\n2. Extract literal anchors: paths, symbols, errors, commands, APIs, config keys.\n3. Resolve anchors into graph identities.\n4. Retrieve graph candidates.\n5. Retrieve memory candidates from typed streams.\n6. Retrieve relevant event episodes.\n7. Expand through bounded graph and memory neighborhoods.\n8. Score candidates.\n9. Deduplicate and compress.\n10. Return a compact bundle with inclusion reasons and expansion handles.\n\nCandidate sources:\n\n- exact path/symbol lookup\n- code graph traversal\n- doc backlinks/outgoing links\n- FTS\n- embeddings\n- event similarity\n- memory links\n- workflow similarity\n- recent active working memory\n\nRanking signals:\n\n- task-type compatibility\n- graph proximity to anchors\n- exact identifier match\n- semantic similarity\n- verification status\n- freshness\n- scope\n- evidence strength\n- contradiction/supersession state\n- past usefulness\n- recent successful reuse\n- user preference compatibility\n- token cost\n\nThe ranker should expose scores and reasons in diagnostic mode. Compact mode should include only enough explanation for an assistant to trust the result.\n\n### 8. Verification Engine\n\nThe verification engine keeps memory honest.\n\nVerification checks:\n\n- linked files still exist\n- linked symbols still exist\n- cited docs still exist\n- linked tests still exist\n- evidence text still matches when exact spans were captured\n- implementation still matches memory claim where deterministic checks are possible\n- contradicted/superseded states remain coherent\n- branch-scoped memory is not leaking into unrelated branches\n- time-bound memory has expired\n\nVerification outputs:\n\n- `verified`\n- `unverified`\n- `in_review`\n- `stale`\n- `contradicted`\n- `superseded`\n- `expired`\n- `invalidated`\n\nVerification must be incremental and tied to workspace changes. Large repos cannot tolerate full rescans for every memory.\n\n### 9. MCP Surface\n\nThe MCP contract should expose high-level assistant workflows rather than forcing clients to compose low-level graph calls.\n","numLines":80,"startLine":354,"totalLines":969}}}
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/R55.log:82:{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MdhRodUbVjaCbWUYJz4N3V","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t//! Memory surfacing discipline for workflow bundles.\n2\t//!\n3\t//! `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md`\n4\t//! `## Non-Negotiable Product Properties` requires:\n5\t//! \"Every stale or contradicted memory is surfaced as such, not hidden behind recency.\"\n6\t//!\n7\t//! `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md`\n8\t//! `## 8. Verification Engine` defines the verification outputs:\n9\t//! `verified`, `unverified`, `in_review`, `stale`, `contradicted`,\n10\t//! `superseded`, `expired`, and `invalidated`.\n11\t//!\n12\t//! `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md`\n13\t//! `## Risks — Stale Memory Leakage` names the control:\n14\t//! \"freshness indexes, graph-change-triggered verification, stale labels\n15\t//! in all memory surfaces, and tests that stale memory cannot rank as trusted.\"\n16\t\n17\tuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\n18\tuse tracing::{debug, error};\n19\t\n20\tuse crate::identity::{Identity, MemoryId};\n21\tuse crate::memory::{Memory, MemoryScope, MemoryVerificationStatus};\n22\tuse crate::retrieval_v1::{RankedCandidate, ScoringContext};\n23\t\n24\t#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\n25\t#[serde(rename_all = \"snake_case\")]\n26\tpub enum BundleSection {\n27\t    Trusted,\n28\t    Stale,\n29\t    Contradicted,\n30\t    Superseded,\n31\t    Expired,\n32\t    Invalidated,\n33\t    InReview,\n34\t    Unverified,\n35\t}\n36\t\n37\t#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\n38\tpub struct LabeledMemory {\n39\t    pub memory_id: MemoryId,\n40\t    pub section: BundleSection,\n41\t    pub label_reason: String,\n42\t    pub content: String,\n43\t}\n44\t\n45\t#[derive(Clone, Debug, Default, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\n46\tpub struct SurfacedBundle {\n47\t    pub trusted: Vec<LabeledMemory>,\n48\t    pub advisory: Vec<LabeledMemory>,\n49\t}\n50\t\n51\t#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\n52\tpub enum SurfacingError {\n53\t    RankerIntegrationNotInitialized { memory_id: String },\n54\t}\n55\t\n56\tpub trait BundleProducer {\n57\t    fn surface(memories: Vec<Memory>) -> SurfacedBundle;\n58\t}\n59\t\n60\tpub struct SurfacingPipeline;\n61\t\n62\timpl BundleProducer for SurfacingPipeline {\n63\t    fn surface(memories: Vec<Memory>) -> SurfacedBundle {\n64\t        Self::partition(memories)\n65\t    }\n66\t}\n67\t\n68\timpl SurfacingPipeline {\n69\t    pub fn partition(memories: Vec<Memory>) -> SurfacedBundle {\n70\t        Self::partition_for_caller(memories, module_path!())\n71\t    }\n72\t\n73\t    pub fn partition_for_caller(\n74\t        memories: Vec<Memory>,\n75\t        caller_module: &'static str,\n76\t    ) -> SurfacedBundle {\n77\t        let mut trusted = Vec::new();\n78\t        let mut advisory = Vec::new();\n79\t\n80\t        for memory in memories {\n81\t            let labeled = Self::label(memory);\n82\t            if labeled.section == BundleSection::Trusted {\n83\t                trusted.push(labeled);\n84\t            } else {\n85\t                advisory.push(labeled);\n86\t            }\n87\t        }\n88\t\n89\t        Self::enforce_trusted_invariant(&mut trusted, caller_module);\n90\t        debug!(\n91\t            caller_module,\n92\t            trusted_count = trusted.len(),\n93\t            advisory_count = advisory.len(),\n94\t            \"surfaced memory bundle partitioned\"\n95\t        );\n96\t        SurfacedBundle { trusted, advisory }\n97\t    }\n98\t\n99\t    pub fn classify(memory: &Memory) -> BundleSection {\n100\t        classify_status(&memory.verification_status)\n101\t    }\n102\t\n103\t    pub fn format_reason(memory: &Memory, section: BundleSection) -> String {\n104\t        let status = memory.verification_status.as_str();\n105\t        let evidence = evidence_reason(memory);\n106\t        match section {\n107\t            BundleSection::Trusted => format!(\"Verified memory; {evidence}\"),\n108\t            BundleSection::Stale => format!(\"Stale memory ({status}); {evidence}\"),\n109\t            BundleSection::Contradicted => format!(\"Contradicted memory ({status}); {evidence}\"),\n110\t            BundleSection::Superseded => format!(\"Superseded memory ({status}); {evidence}\"),\n111\t            BundleSection::Expired => format!(\"Expired memory ({status}); {evidence}\"),\n112\t            BundleSection::Invalidated => format!(\"Invalidated memory ({status}); {evidence}\"),\n113\t            BundleSection::InReview => format!(\"Memory is still in review ({status}); {evidence}\"),\n114\t            BundleSection::Unverified => format!(\"Unverified memory ({status}); {evidence}\"),\n115\t        }\n116\t    }\n117\t\n118\t    pub fn trusted_ranked_top_n(\n119\t        ranked: Vec<RankedCandidate>,\n120\t        ctx: &ScoringContext,\n121\t        top_n: usize,\n122\t    ) -> Vec<RankedCandidate> {\n123\t        ranked\n124\t            .into_iter()\n125\t            .filter(|candidate| ranked_candidate_is_trusted_memory(candidate, ctx))\n126\t            .take(top_n)\n127\t            .collect()\n128\t    }\n129\t\n130\t    #[cfg(test)]\n131\t    pub(crate) fn enforce_trusted_invariant_for_test(\n132\t        trusted: &mut Vec<LabeledMemory>,\n133\t        caller_module: &'static str,\n134\t    ) {\n135\t        Self::enforce_trusted_invariant(trusted, caller_module);\n136\t    }\n137\t\n138\t    fn label(memory: Memory) -> LabeledMemory {\n139\t        let section = Self::classify(&memory);\n140\t        let label_reason = Self::format_reason(&memory, section);\n141\t        LabeledMemory {\n142\t            memory_id: memory_id(&memory),\n143\t            section,\n144\t            label_reason,\n145\t            content: memory.content,\n146\t        }\n147\t    }\n148\t\n149\t    fn enforce_trusted_invariant(trusted: &mut Vec<LabeledMemory>, caller_module: &'static str) {\n150\t        #[cfg(debug_assertions)]\n151\t        {\n152\t            if let Some(leaked) = trusted\n153\t                .iter()\n154\t                .find(|memory| memory.section != BundleSection::Trusted)\n155\t            {\n156\t                panic!(\n157\t                    \"stale_in_trusted_bundle memory_id={} status={:?} caller_module={}\",\n158\t                    leaked.memory_id, leaked.section, caller_module\n159\t                );\n160\t            }\n161\t        }\n162\t\n163\t        #[cfg(not(debug_assertions))]\n164\t        {\n165\t            trusted.retain(|memory| {\n166\t                let is_trusted = memory.section == BundleSection::Trusted;\n167\t                if !is_trusted {\n168\t                    error!(\n169\t                        memory_id = %memory.memory_id,\n170\t                        status = ?memory.section,\n171\t                        caller_module,\n172\t                        \"stale_in_trusted_bundle\"\n173\t                    );\n174\t                }\n175\t                is_trusted\n176\t            });\n177\t        }\n178\t    }\n179\t}\n180\t\n181\tpub fn classify_status(status: &MemoryVerificationStatus) -> BundleSection {\n182\t    match status {\n183\t        MemoryVerificationStatus::Verified => BundleSection::Trusted,\n184\t        MemoryVerificationStatus::Unverified => BundleSection::Unverified,\n185\t        MemoryVerificationStatus::InReview => BundleSection::InReview,\n186\t        MemoryVerificationStatus::Stale => BundleSection::Stale,\n187\t        MemoryVerificationStatus::Contradicted => BundleSection::Contradicted,\n188\t        MemoryVerificationStatus::Superseded => BundleSection::Superseded,\n189\t        MemoryVerificationStatus::Expired => BundleSection::Expired,\n190\t        MemoryVerificationStatus::Invalidated => BundleSection::Invalidated,\n191\t    }\n192\t}\n193\t\n194\tfn ranked_candidate_is_trusted_memory(candidate: &RankedCandidate, ctx: &ScoringContext) -> bool {\n195\t    let Identity::Memory(memory_id) = &candidate.candidate.identity else {\n196\t        return true;\n197\t    };\n198\t    ctx.memory_metadata\n199\t        .get(&candidate.candidate.identity.to_string())\n200\t        .map(|metadata| metadata.verification_status == MemoryVerificationStatus::Verified)\n201\t        .unwrap_or_else(|| {\n202\t            error!(\n203\t                memory_id = %memory_id,\n204\t                \"ranker_integration_not_initialized\"\n205\t            );\n206\t            false\n207\t        })\n208\t}\n209\t\n210\tfn memory_id(memory: &Memory) -> MemoryId {\n211\t    MemoryId {\n212\t        workspace_id: memory\n213\t            .workspace_id\n214\t            .clone()\n215\t            .unwrap_or_else(|| \"unknown\".to_string()),\n216\t        ulid: memory.id.clone(),\n217\t    }\n218\t}\n219\t\n220\tfn evidence_reason(memory: &Memory) -> String {\n221\t    let stale_reason = memory\n222\t        .stale_reason\n223\t        .as_deref()\n224\t        .unwrap_or(\"no verifier reason recorded\");\n225\t    let location = memory\n226\t        .linked_files\n227\t        .first()\n228\t        .map(|file| format!(\"file `{file}`\"))\n229\t        .unwrap_or_else(|| \"no linked file\".to_string());\n230\t    let scope = format_scope(&memory.scope, memory.branch.as_deref());\n231\t    format!(\"{stale_reason}; {location}; {scope}\")\n232\t}\n233\t\n234\tfn format_scope(scope: &MemoryScope, branch: Option<&str>) -> String {\n235\t    match (scope, branch) {\n236\t        (MemoryScope::Branch, Some(branch)) => format!(\"scope branch `{branch}`\"),\n237\t        (MemoryScope::Branch, None) => \"scope branch\".to_string(),\n238\t        (MemoryScope::Session, _) => \"scope session\".to_string(),\n239\t        (MemoryScope::Repo, _) => \"scope repo\".to_string(),\n240\t        (MemoryScope::Organization, _) => \"scope organization\".to_string(),\n241\t    }\n242\t}\n243\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"623701ab-dc49-4054-96ef-292da32369e2","uuid":"a896d632-1861-4ee7-9bcf-17bac6935dae","timestamp":"2026-05-17T13:10:25.807Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/verification/surfacing.rs","content":"//! Memory surfacing discipline for workflow bundles.\n//!\n//! `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md`\n//! `## Non-Negotiable Product Properties` requires:\n//! \"Every stale or contradicted memory is surfaced as such, not hidden behind recency.\"\n//!\n//! `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md`\n//! `## 8. Verification Engine` defines the verification outputs:\n//! `verified`, `unverified`, `in_review`, `stale`, `contradicted`,\n//! `superseded`, `expired`, and `invalidated`.\n//!\n//! `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md`\n//! `## Risks — Stale Memory Leakage` names the control:\n//! \"freshness indexes, graph-change-triggered verification, stale labels\n//! in all memory surfaces, and tests that stale memory cannot rank as trusted.\"\n\nuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\nuse tracing::{debug, error};\n\nuse crate::identity::{Identity, MemoryId};\nuse crate::memory::{Memory, MemoryScope, MemoryVerificationStatus};\nuse crate::retrieval_v1::{RankedCandidate, ScoringContext};\n\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\n#[serde(rename_all = \"snake_case\")]\npub enum BundleSection {\n    Trusted,\n    Stale,\n    Contradicted,\n    Superseded,\n    Expired,\n    Invalidated,\n    InReview,\n    Unverified,\n}\n\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\npub struct LabeledMemory {\n    pub memory_id: MemoryId,\n    pub section: BundleSection,\n    pub label_reason: String,\n    pub content: String,\n}\n\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, Default, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\npub struct SurfacedBundle {\n    pub trusted: Vec<LabeledMemory>,\n    pub advisory: Vec<LabeledMemory>,\n}\n\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub enum SurfacingError {\n    RankerIntegrationNotInitialized { memory_id: String },\n}\n\npub trait BundleProducer {\n    fn surface(memories: Vec<Memory>) -> SurfacedBundle;\n}\n\npub struct SurfacingPipeline;\n\nimpl BundleProducer for SurfacingPipeline {\n    fn surface(memories: Vec<Memory>) -> SurfacedBundle {\n        Self::partition(memories)\n    }\n}\n\nimpl SurfacingPipeline {\n    pub fn partition(memories: Vec<Memory>) -> SurfacedBundle {\n        Self::partition_for_caller(memories, module_path!())\n    }\n\n    pub fn partition_for_caller(\n        memories: Vec<Memory>,\n        caller_module: &'static str,\n    ) -> SurfacedBundle {\n        let mut trusted = Vec::new();\n        let mut advisory = Vec::new();\n\n        for memory in memories {\n            let labeled = Self::label(memory);\n            if labeled.section == BundleSection::Trusted {\n                trusted.push(labeled);\n            } else {\n                advisory.push(labeled);\n            }\n        }\n\n        Self::enforce_trusted_invariant(&mut trusted, caller_module);\n        debug!(\n            caller_module,\n            trusted_count = trusted.len(),\n            advisory_count = advisory.len(),\n            \"surfaced memory bundle partitioned\"\n        );\n        SurfacedBundle { trusted, advisory }\n    }\n\n    pub fn classify(memory: &Memory) -> BundleSection {\n        classify_status(&memory.verification_status)\n    }\n\n    pub fn format_reason(memory: &Memory, section: BundleSection) -> String {\n        let status = memory.verification_status.as_str();\n        let evidence = evidence_reason(memory);\n        match section {\n            BundleSection::Trusted => format!(\"Verified memory; {evidence}\"),\n            BundleSection::Stale => format!(\"Stale memory ({status}); {evidence}\"),\n            BundleSection::Contradicted => format!(\"Contradicted memory ({status}); {evidence}\"),\n            BundleSection::Superseded => format!(\"Superseded memory ({status}); {evidence}\"),\n            BundleSection::Expired => format!(\"Expired memory ({status}); {evidence}\"),\n            BundleSection::Invalidated => format!(\"Invalidated memory ({status}); {evidence}\"),\n            BundleSection::InReview => format!(\"Memory is still in review ({status}); {evidence}\"),\n            BundleSection::Unverified => format!(\"Unverified memory ({status}); {evidence}\"),\n        }\n    }\n\n    pub fn trusted_ranked_top_n(\n        ranked: Vec<RankedCandidate>,\n        ctx: &ScoringContext,\n        top_n: usize,\n    ) -> Vec<RankedCandidate> {\n        ranked\n            .into_iter()\n            .filter(|candidate| ranked_candidate_is_trusted_memory(candidate, ctx))\n            .take(top_n)\n            .collect()\n    }\n\n    #[cfg(test)]\n    pub(crate) fn enforce_trusted_invariant_for_test(\n        trusted: &mut Vec<LabeledMemory>,\n        caller_module: &'static str,\n    ) {\n        Self::enforce_trusted_invariant(trusted, caller_module);\n    }\n\n    fn label(memory: Memory) -> LabeledMemory {\n        let section = Self::classify(&memory);\n        let label_reason = Self::format_reason(&memory, section);\n        LabeledMemory {\n            memory_id: memory_id(&memory),\n            section,\n            label_reason,\n            content: memory.content,\n        }\n    }\n\n    fn enforce_trusted_invariant(trusted: &mut Vec<LabeledMemory>, caller_module: &'static str) {\n        #[cfg(debug_assertions)]\n        {\n            if let Some(leaked) = trusted\n                .iter()\n                .find(|memory| memory.section != BundleSection::Trusted)\n            {\n                panic!(\n                    \"stale_in_trusted_bundle memory_id={} status={:?} caller_module={}\",\n                    leaked.memory_id, leaked.section, caller_module\n                );\n            }\n        }\n\n        #[cfg(not(debug_assertions))]\n        {\n            trusted.retain(|memory| {\n                let is_trusted = memory.section == BundleSection::Trusted;\n                if !is_trusted {\n                    error!(\n                        memory_id = %memory.memory_id,\n                        status = ?memory.section,\n                        caller_module,\n                        \"stale_in_trusted_bundle\"\n                    );\n                }\n                is_trusted\n            });\n        }\n    }\n}\n\npub fn classify_status(status: &MemoryVerificationStatus) -> BundleSection {\n    match status {\n        MemoryVerificationStatus::Verified => BundleSection::Trusted,\n        MemoryVerificationStatus::Unverified => BundleSection::Unverified,\n        MemoryVerificationStatus::InReview => BundleSection::InReview,\n        MemoryVerificationStatus::Stale => BundleSection::Stale,\n        MemoryVerificationStatus::Contradicted => BundleSection::Contradicted,\n        MemoryVerificationStatus::Superseded => BundleSection::Superseded,\n        MemoryVerificationStatus::Expired => BundleSection::Expired,\n        MemoryVerificationStatus::Invalidated => BundleSection::Invalidated,\n    }\n}\n\nfn ranked_candidate_is_trusted_memory(candidate: &RankedCandidate, ctx: &ScoringContext) -> bool {\n    let Identity::Memory(memory_id) = &candidate.candidate.identity else {\n        return true;\n    };\n    ctx.memory_metadata\n        .get(&candidate.candidate.identity.to_string())\n        .map(|metadata| metadata.verification_status == MemoryVerificationStatus::Verified)\n        .unwrap_or_else(|| {\n            error!(\n                memory_id = %memory_id,\n                \"ranker_integration_not_initialized\"\n            );\n            false\n        })\n}\n\nfn memory_id(memory: &Memory) -> MemoryId {\n    MemoryId {\n        workspace_id: memory\n            .workspace_id\n            .clone()\n            .unwrap_or_else(|| \"unknown\".to_string()),\n        ulid: memory.id.clone(),\n    }\n}\n\nfn evidence_reason(memory: &Memory) -> String {\n    let stale_reason = memory\n        .stale_reason\n        .as_deref()\n        .unwrap_or(\"no verifier reason recorded\");\n    let location = memory\n        .linked_files\n        .first()\n        .map(|file| format!(\"file `{file}`\"))\n        .unwrap_or_else(|| \"no linked file\".to_string());\n    let scope = format_scope(&memory.scope, memory.branch.as_deref());\n    format!(\"{stale_reason}; {location}; {scope}\")\n}\n\nfn format_scope(scope: &MemoryScope, branch: Option<&str>) -> String {\n    match (scope, branch) {\n        (MemoryScope::Branch, Some(branch)) => format!(\"scope branch `{branch}`\"),\n        (MemoryScope::Branch, None) => \"scope branch\".to_string(),\n        (MemoryScope::Session, _) => \"scope session\".to_string(),\n        (MemoryScope::Repo, _) => \"scope repo\".to_string(),\n        (MemoryScope::Organization, _) => \"scope organization\".to_string(),\n    }\n}\n","numLines":243,"startLine":1,"totalLines":243}}}
